/*--------------------------------*- C++ -*----------------------------------*\
  ZERO GRAVITY, and it is a modelling statement, not a convenience: the manual
  describes FORCED convection ("Incompressible, turbulent flow with heat
  convection and reattachment") and gives no orientation and no buoyancy
  parameter. With g = 0 the buoyant term vanishes identically, p_rgh == p, and
  the temperature field is transported without feeding back into the momentum
  equation -- which is what "fluid properties are considered constant" means.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
FoamFile { version 2.0; format ascii; class uniformDimensionedVectorField; object g; }
dimensions [0 1 -2 0 0 0 0];
value (0 0 0);
